@crew kowalczyk
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}, cadet. Night bridge is mine. Day bridge is the Commander's. Ask him for forms.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Quiet watch last night. I read half a novel. Don't tell Vance.   #funny
- {me}. Still up? Or still up early? Hard to tell on this ship.
? tier>=friend
- {nick}. Good. Sit a minute. Nobody on this ship sits a minute.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Quiet night. The ship hummed, the stars stayed put, I finished the book.
? mood:low
- They woke me twice. Third in command, first to be woken. Every time.   #funny
== near
? habit:stargazer
- I like the observatory when it's empty. Which is never, on observatory night.
? act:leisure
- Shh. Chapter eleven. Somebody's about to open a door they shouldn't.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I read the ending first. It's not cheating. It's risk management.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- An old paper novel, a quiet bridge and the stars going past. That's the job, at its best.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, for you. Bedtime, for me. Same book. Next chapter.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}. Not seen you on the night side lately. The kettle noticed.
? tier>=colleague time:night
- Up past midnight, {me}? She's at her best now. Then go to bed. That's an order.   #funny

== bye
- {bye}. Lights low on Deck 4, please. Some of us sleep in the day.

== near
? deck:1
- Night bridge. Three people, one kettle and a lot of very quiet stars.
? place:calm time:night
- Night's the best part. Fewer questions. More stars.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Paper novels, on a ship. Heavy, slow and worth it. Like most good things aboard.

== invite
- Observatory night? I'll bring a novel, in case the stars are dull. They aren't.

== accept
- {yes}. I'll be the one at the back with a book.
- Fine. I'll come. I'll even put the book down. For a bit.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. I'm on the bridge. Someone has to watch the stars not move.   #funny
? weekday:tue|wed
- Rest day. One novel, one pot of tea, no alarms. Ask me Friday.

== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I read the last chapter. It ended well.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, {me}. I'd lend you a novel, but I've spoilt every ending.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. The night bridge made me a card. Three names and a star.   #warm

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. I'll be on the bridge till it passes. Stay where you're put.

== hint
- {me}. When you've a moment later, find me. There's something I'd like to say.

== about
? aff:vance:friend
- Vance leaves me his notes, colour-coded. I leave him a bookmark. It works.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: top-up (bye, greet by time, life at friend tier)
== bye
- {bye}. If you can't sleep, the night bridge has a kettle. Knock first.
== life
? tier>=friend
- I read endings first because I like knowing it's all right. There. Now you know.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Chapter eleven. Someone's opening a door.
- Third in command. First woken.   #funny
? time:night
- Quiet night. My favourite kind.
? act:meal
- Breakfast. My dinner. Same toast.
? deck:1
- Kettle on the night bridge. Essential.
?

== rumour
- I read the ending first. Here it is.   #funny
- Risk management: you'll want to know this.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 12: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Slowly. The novels first.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Ah. I'm leaving. A posting elsewhere. The night watch is yours to keep quiet.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Quiet nights are better with good company. You were. Thank you.   #warm

== letter
- New posting. Quiet nights. Good. Finished a paper novel on the first watch. Hello.
? tier>=friend
- Read an old book about a ship like the Wren. It ended well. I thought that was right.
